Description: Auto DJ requests: [Library],AutoDjAddRequest
 A request (a dedication, a guest's wish) goes where it fits best by key and
 tempo among the next N tracks of the Auto DJ queue (Preferences > Auto DJ >
 Requests, default 5), after the track a running Auto DJ has cued already and
 never at a track loaded in a deck. A track in the queue already moves up
 instead (never down), so the same control prioritizes a queued track, also
 from the Auto DJ view. "Play requests in the order they came" (default off)
 keeps a request after the earlier ones. Requests are highlighted in the
 queue (amber, bold) until they leave it; the highlight is not stored.
 The slot choice is harmonicRequestSlot() in library/autodj/harmonicorder.h
 (from 0006), unit tested; the control is in the controller learning wizard's
 Library menu. New PlaylistDAO::AutoDJSendLoc::REQUEST.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
